IMPORT prelude

-- Choice of Court Agreements Act 2016 (Singapore) -- when a clause choosing a court is an exclusive choice of court agreement
-- (s 3), when the Act applies to it (ss 4, 6, 8, 9, 10, 24), what a Singapore court must do with it (ss 11, 12), and when the
-- General Division of the High Court must or may refuse to recognise or enforce a foreign judgment or judicial settlement
-- (ss 2, 13 to 16, 20). Also ss 2(2), (3) (High Court designations and the SICC) and s 5 (the clause survives the contract).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on
-- 31 December 2021"), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CCAA2016.txt (SSO version current as at 1 October 2026,
-- retrieved 1 October 2026). The latest amendment annotated is Act 40 of 2019 (Supreme Court of Judicature (Amendment) Act 2019,
-- in force 2 January 2021), marked [40/2019] throughout Part 3.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0044 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. The Act is short (24 sections), so this row covers most of its operative content. Not encoded:
-- s 2(4) (multi-unit States), s 7, s 9(4) and every other power to make regulations (none was retrieved, so "prescribed"
-- grounds are absent), s 11(3) to (5), s 15(3) (re-application after an appeal), s 17 (rulings on preliminary questions in the
-- foreign proceedings), s 18 (insurance judgments), s 19 (severable parts, beyond a comment), ss 21 to 23, and which States are
-- Contracting States (a fact, taken as an input).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Choice of Court Agreements Act 2016`

§§ `2(2), (3) -- a clause naming the High Court`

-- s 2(2): where "the High Court" is designated, the designation is construed "(a) as a designation of the General Division of
-- the High Court; and (b) as including the Singapore International Commercial Court, unless a contrary intention appears in the
-- agreement". s 2(3): the same for a designation of the General Division.
DECLARE `Named court` IS ONE OF
    `the High Court`
    `the General Division of the High Court`
    `the State Courts`
    `the courts of England`

GIVEN `the named court` IS A `Named court`, `the agreement shows a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the designation includes the SICC` IF
    CONSIDER `the named court`
    WHEN `the High Court` THEN NOT `the agreement shows a contrary intention`
    WHEN `the General Division of the High Court` THEN NOT `the agreement shows a contrary intention`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `2(1) -- judgments and judicial settlements`

-- s 2(1): "judgment" means "(a) a final court decision (by whatever name called) on the merits, a consent order, a consent
-- judgment or a judgment given by default; or (b) a determination by a court of any costs or expenses relating to" one.
-- "judicial settlement" means a contract approved by, or concluded before, a foreign court in the course of proceedings, between
-- the parties, ending the proceedings and recorded by the court in an official document, "but (b) does not include a consent
-- order or consent judgment". s 10(1): "This Act does not apply to any interim measure of protection."
DECLARE `Court outcome` IS ONE OF
    `a final decision on the merits`
    `a default judgment`
    `a consent order`
    `a consent judgment`
    `a costs determination`
    `a settlement contract recorded by the court`
    `an interim injunction`

DECLARE Route IS ONE OF
    `recognition and enforcement as a judgment`
    `enforcement as a judicial settlement`
    `not under this Act`

GIVEN `the outcome` IS A `Court outcome`
GIVETH A Route
`the route under Part 3` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the outcome`
    WHEN `a settlement contract recorded by the court` THEN `enforcement as a judicial settlement`
    WHEN `an interim injunction` THEN `not under this Act`
    OTHERWISE `recognition and enforcement as a judgment`

§§ `3 -- exclusive choice of court agreement`

-- s 3(1): an agreement between 2 or more parties that "(a) is concluded or documented -- (i) in writing; or (ii) by any other means
-- of communication that renders the information communicated accessible so as to be usable for subsequent reference; and (b)
-- designates ... the courts, or one or more specific courts, of one Contracting State to the exclusion of the jurisdiction of any
-- other court". s 3(2): an agreement meeting (a) and designating the courts of one Contracting State "is deemed to be an exclusive
-- choice of court agreement, unless the parties to the agreement expressly provide otherwise".
DECLARE Matter IS ONE OF
    `a commercial supply contract`
    `a loan facility`
    `an insurance contract`
    `a contract with a consumer`
    `an employment contract`
    `a divorce or maintenance claim`
    `a succession or probate claim`
    `an insolvency`
    `carriage of passengers and goods`
    `a competition law claim`
    `a personal injury claim`
    `a non-contractual tort damaging property`
    `a tenancy of immovable property`
    `the validity of a patent`
    `a patent infringement outside any contract`
    `breach of a patent licence`
    `the validity of a copyright`
    `an arbitration`

DECLARE Dispute HAS
    `the matter` IS A Matter
    `the matter arises only as a preliminary question or defence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties reside in the same Contracting State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `everything else is connected only with that State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in writing or an accessible record` IS A BOOLEAN
    `designates the courts of one Contracting State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `says other courts are excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties expressly made it non-exclusive` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Singapore court is chosen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `concluded before 1 October 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
    `concluded before the Convention bound the chosen State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim is for an interim measure` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the dispute` IS A Dispute
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement is exclusive` IF
        `the dispute`'s `in writing or an accessible record`
    AND `the dispute`'s `designates the courts of one Contracting State`
    AND (    `the dispute`'s `says other courts are excluded`
         OR  (NOT `the dispute`'s `the parties expressly made it non-exclusive`))

§§ `4(1), 6 -- international case and residence`

-- s 4(1): for Part 2, "a case is an international case unless -- (a) the parties to the case reside in the same Contracting State;
-- and (b) the relationship of the parties and all other elements relevant to the dispute (other than the location of the chosen
-- court) are connected only with that Contracting State". (Part 3 cases are always international, s 4(2).)
GIVEN `the dispute` IS A Dispute
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the case is international for Part 2` IF
    NOT (    `the dispute`'s `the parties reside in the same Contracting State`
         AND `the dispute`'s `everything else is connected only with that State`)

-- s 6: a person other than an individual is resident in a State if "(a) the person has its statutory seat in that State; (b) the
-- person was incorporated or formed under the law of that State; (c) the person has its central administration in that State;
-- or (d) the person has its principal place of business in that State". Any one suffices, so a company may reside in several.
GIVEN `statutory seat there` IS A BOOLEAN, `incorporated there` IS A BOOLEAN, `central administration there` IS A BOOLEAN, `principal place of business there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company resides in the State` IF
        `statutory seat there`
    OR  `incorporated there`
    OR  `central administration there`
    OR  `principal place of business there`

§§ `5 -- the clause is independent of the contract`

-- s 5: where the agreement forms part of a contract "(a) the agreement is to be treated as independent of the other terms of the
-- contract; and (b) the validity of the agreement cannot be challenged solely on the ground that the contract is not valid".
GIVEN `the main contract is invalid` IS A BOOLEAN, `the clause has a defect of its own` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the clause can be held invalid` IF
    `the clause has a defect of its own`

§§ `8, 9, 10, 24 -- when the Act applies`

-- s 9(1): the Act does not apply if "(a) any party to the agreement is an individual who acts primarily in the capacity of a
-- consumer; or (b) the agreement relates to a contract of employment or a collective agreement". s 9(2) lists excluded matters:
-- (b) family law, (c) succession, (d) insolvency, (e) "the carriage of passengers and goods", (g) competition, (i) personal injury
-- or death, (j) non-contractual tort damaging tangible property, (k) rights in rem in or tenancies of immovable property, (m) the
-- validity and (n) infringement of IP "(other than copyright and related rights)" -- except infringement proceedings that could
-- have been brought for breach of a contract between the parties relating to that right -- among others. s 9(3): arbitration.
-- s 9(5): a s 9(2) matter raised "as a preliminary question or defence, and not as an object of the proceedings, does not prevent
-- this Act from applying". s 9(6): an insurance proceeding is not excluded "by reason only that the contract relates to" an
-- excluded matter.
GIVEN `the subject` IS A Matter, `only a preliminary question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the matter is excluded` IF
    CONSIDER `the subject`
    WHEN `a contract with a consumer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an employment contract` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an arbitration` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a divorce or maintenance claim` THEN NOT `only a preliminary question`
    WHEN `a succession or probate claim` THEN NOT `only a preliminary question`
    WHEN `an insolvency` THEN NOT `only a preliminary question`
    WHEN `carriage of passengers and goods` THEN NOT `only a preliminary question`
    WHEN `a competition law claim` THEN NOT `only a preliminary question`
    WHEN `a personal injury claim` THEN NOT `only a preliminary question`
    WHEN `a non-contractual tort damaging property` THEN NOT `only a preliminary question`
    WHEN `a tenancy of immovable property` THEN NOT `only a preliminary question`
    WHEN `the validity of a patent` THEN NOT `only a preliminary question`
    WHEN `a patent infringement outside any contract` THEN NOT `only a preliminary question`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 24(1): the Act does not apply to an agreement designating a Singapore court "if the agreement is concluded before 1 October
-- 2016"; (2) nor to one designating a court of another Contracting State "if the agreement is concluded before the Convention
-- enters into force in that Contracting State". s 10(1): nor to an interim measure of protection (and s 10(2) leaves a party free
-- to apply to a Singapore court for one).
GIVEN `the dispute` IS A Dispute
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement predates the Act` IF
        (`the dispute`'s `a Singapore court is chosen` AND `the dispute`'s `concluded before 1 October 2016`)
    OR  ((NOT `the dispute`'s `a Singapore court is chosen`) AND `the dispute`'s `concluded before the Convention bound the chosen State`)

-- s 8: "this Act applies in every international case where there is an exclusive choice of court agreement concluded in a civil or
-- commercial matter", subject to ss 9, 10 and 22.
GIVEN `the dispute` IS A Dispute
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies` IF
        `the case is international for Part 2` `the dispute`
    AND `the agreement is exclusive` `the dispute`
    AND (NOT `the matter is excluded` (`the dispute`'s `the matter`) (`the dispute`'s `the matter arises only as a preliminary question or defence`))
    AND (NOT `the agreement predates the Act` `the dispute`)
    AND (NOT `the dispute`'s `the claim is for an interim measure`)

§§ `11 -- Singapore is the chosen court`

-- s 11(1): a designated Singapore court "has jurisdiction to decide the dispute, unless the agreement is null and void under the
-- law of Singapore". (2): it "cannot decline to exercise jurisdiction on the ground that the dispute should be decided in a court
-- of another State" -- forum non conveniens is not available. (Regulations under s 11(3) could add grounds; none retrieved.)
GIVEN `the dispute` IS A Dispute, `void under Singapore law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Singapore court must hear the dispute` IF
        `the Act applies` `the dispute`
    AND `the dispute`'s `a Singapore court is chosen`
    AND (NOT `void under Singapore law`)

§§ `12 -- a foreign court is the chosen court`

-- s 12(1): "Despite any other written law or rule of law", if no Singapore court is chosen, "a Singapore court must stay or dismiss
-- any case or proceeding to which the agreement applies, unless" it determines that (a) the agreement is null and void under the
-- law of the State of the chosen court; (b) a party lacked capacity under the law of Singapore; (c) giving effect to it "would lead
-- to a manifest injustice or would be manifestly contrary to the public policy of Singapore"; (d) it "cannot reasonably be
-- performed for exceptional reasons beyond the control of the parties"; or (e) the chosen court has decided not to hear the case.
-- (2): other grounds for a stay are unaffected.
GIVEN `the dispute` IS A Dispute, `void under the chosen State's law` IS A BOOLEAN, `a party lacked capacity` IS A BOOLEAN, `manifest injustice or public policy` IS A BOOLEAN, `cannot reasonably be performed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the chosen court declined the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Singapore court must stay or dismiss` IF
        `the Act applies` `the dispute`
    AND (NOT `the dispute`'s `a Singapore court is chosen`)
    AND (NOT `void under the chosen State's law`)
    AND (NOT `a party lacked capacity`)
    AND (NOT `manifest injustice or public policy`)
    AND (NOT `cannot reasonably be performed`)
    AND (NOT `the chosen court declined the case`)

§§ `13 to 16 -- recognising and enforcing a foreign judgment`

-- s 2(1): a "foreign judgment" is a judgment of a court of a Contracting State other than Singapore that is "(a) a chosen court; or
-- (b) a court to which a chosen court has transferred" the case. s 13(2): it "(a) is to be recognised only if the judgment has
-- effect in the State of origin; and (b) is to be enforced only if the judgment is enforceable in the State of origin". s 13(3):
-- the court "must not review the merits". s 13(4): if the requirements are met the court "must recognise, or recognise and enforce"
-- it, except as provided for refusal.
--
-- s 14 (MUST refuse): (a) the defendant was not notified of the originating document "in sufficient time to enable the defendant to
-- defend the proceedings, unless -- (i) the law of the State of origin allows the notification to be challenged; and (ii) the
-- defendant had entered an appearance and presented the defendant's case without challenging the notification"; (b) "obtained by
-- fraud in connection with a matter of procedure"; (c) "manifestly incompatible with the public policy of Singapore".
--
-- s 15(1) (MAY refuse): (a) the agreement is null and void under the law of the chosen State, "unless the chosen court has
-- determined that the agreement is valid"; (b) a party lacked capacity under Singapore law; (c) service incompatible with
-- Singapore's fundamental principles; (d) inconsistent with a Singapore judgment between the same parties; (e) inconsistent with an
-- earlier recognisable foreign judgment between the same parties on the same cause of action. s 15(2): may refuse or postpone while
-- the judgment is under review or appeal, or the time to appeal has not expired. s 15(4): may refuse against a party who "objected in
-- a timely manner" to a discretionary transfer. s 16(1): may refuse "if, and to the extent that" damages exceed "compensation for
-- the actual loss or harm suffered" (including exemplary or punitive damages); s 16(2) the court must weigh whether they cover costs.
-- s 16 and s 19 (severable parts) operate to an EXTENT; this encoding reports only that the court may refuse.
DECLARE `Foreign judgment` HAS
    `from the chosen court or a court it transferred to` IS A BOOLEAN
    `from a Contracting State other than Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has effect in the State of origin` IS A BOOLEAN
    `enforceable in the State of origin` IS A BOOLEAN
    `defendant not notified in sufficient time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `origin law allowed a challenge and the defendant defended without one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `obtained by procedural fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
    `manifestly against Singapore public policy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `agreement void under chosen State law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the chosen court held the agreement valid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a party lacked capacity under Singapore law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `served contrary to Singapore principles` IS A BOOLEAN
    `inconsistent with a Singapore judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `inconsistent with an earlier recognisable foreign judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `under appeal or appeal time running` IS A BOOLEAN
    `transferred over the defendant's timely objection` IS A BOOLEAN
    `damages exceed actual loss` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Outcome IS ONE OF
    `must recognise and enforce`
    `must recognise but not enforce`
    `must enforce the settlement`
    `must refuse`
    `may refuse`
    `outside Part 3`

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A `Foreign judgment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a ground to refuse is mandatory` IF
        (    `the judgment`'s `defendant not notified in sufficient time`
         AND (NOT `the judgment`'s `origin law allowed a challenge and the defendant defended without one`))
    OR  `the judgment`'s `obtained by procedural fraud`
    OR  `the judgment`'s `manifestly against Singapore public policy`

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A `Foreign judgment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a ground to refuse is discretionary` IF
        (`the judgment`'s `agreement void under chosen State law` AND (NOT `the judgment`'s `the chosen court held the agreement valid`))
    OR  `the judgment`'s `a party lacked capacity under Singapore law`
    OR  `the judgment`'s `served contrary to Singapore principles`
    OR  `the judgment`'s `inconsistent with a Singapore judgment`
    OR  `the judgment`'s `inconsistent with an earlier recognisable foreign judgment`
    OR  `the judgment`'s `under appeal or appeal time running`
    OR  `the judgment`'s `transferred over the defendant's timely objection`
    OR  `the judgment`'s `damages exceed actual loss`

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A `Foreign judgment`
GIVETH AN Outcome
`what the General Division must do` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the judgment`'s `from the chosen court or a court it transferred to` AND `the judgment`'s `from a Contracting State other than Singapore`)
    THEN `outside Part 3`
    ELSE IF NOT `the judgment`'s `has effect in the State of origin`
         THEN `must refuse`
         ELSE IF `a ground to refuse is mandatory` `the judgment`
              THEN `must refuse`
              ELSE IF `a ground to refuse is discretionary` `the judgment`
                   THEN `may refuse`
                   ELSE IF `the judgment`'s `enforceable in the State of origin`
                        THEN `must recognise and enforce`
                        ELSE `must recognise but not enforce`

§§ `20 -- judicial settlements`

-- s 20(2): the General Division "must enforce a judicial settlement only if -- (a) the judicial settlement -- (i) was approved by a
-- chosen court ...; or (ii) was concluded before the chosen court ... in the course of proceedings before that court; and (b) the
-- judicial settlement is enforceable in the same manner and to the same extent as a judgment in the State of origin". (3) it must
-- refuse in any circumstance in which a foreign judgment MUST be refused; (4) it may refuse in any circumstance in which a foreign
-- judgment MAY be refused. A settlement is enforced, never "recognised": s 20 speaks only of enforcement.
GIVEN `approved by or concluded before the chosen court` IS A BOOLEAN, `enforceable as a judgment at origin` IS A BOOLEAN, `a mandatory ground applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `a discretionary ground applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Outcome
`what the General Division must do with the settlement` MEANS
    IF NOT (`approved by or concluded before the chosen court` AND `enforceable as a judgment at origin`)
    THEN `must refuse`
    ELSE IF `a mandatory ground applies`
         THEN `must refuse`
         ELSE IF `a discretionary ground applies`
              THEN `may refuse`
              ELSE `must enforce the settlement`
